      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{7}{3x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the limit using the algebra of limits,  as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{7}{3x} & =\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the fact that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(\\frac{1}{x})=-\\infty ,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}(\\frac{1}{x})=\\infty .\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{1}{x})=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{x}=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
